I found the reason is DynamicSlice's input_size is 3, and we should get the inputs from index 0-2 rather then 3:
caffe2/onnx/backend.cc
@@ -1080,7 +1108,7 @@ Caffe2Ops Caffe2Backend::CreateDynamicSlice(
   // arguments to the caffe2 Slice operator.
   std::string axes_tensor;
   if (onnx_node->node.input_size() > 2) {
-    axes_tensor = onnx_node->node.input(3);
+    axes_tensor = onnx_node->node.input(2);
   } else {
     axes_tensor = dummy_->NewDummyName();
     auto* c2_op = ret.ops.Add();


To Reproduce
Steps to reproduce the behavior:
1.Original model:    tensorflow's inceptionv4 model
2.convert to onnx
3.onnx model convert to caffe2:
convert-onnx-to-caffe2 ./inception_v4/inception_v4.onnx --output ./inception_v4/onnx_predict_net.pb --init-net-output ./inception_v4/onnx_init_net.pb


Expected behavior
produce onnx_predict_net.pb and onnx_init_net.pb successfully.
